                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "so being a Forklift operator AND a gamer i think i'm qualified to review this game, so first of all the physics in this game are rubbish, the propper way to pick up cargo is to align your truck, then drive forward until your gate hits the cargo (this is ofcourse done very slowly and depending on what you are picking up) but even slightly toutching the cargo will cause it to fly backwards... then you lift it a few inches of the gound before tilting your forks bakwards so the cargo wont slipp of, doing so ingame causes your forks to tilt bacwards BUT your cargo does not, like the pallet was made from ice and attatched to the wall. ok so you have flimsily picked up you cargo now what? well when you have picked up the cargo your turn rate falls into the \"overloaded cargo ship\" range, what should have been a simply 2 turn manouver suddenly became a 19 turn manouver \"jikes\" this could have been a nice little forklift sim but the games engin does not work properly making this a disaster",
